<p>Eh, in my opinion, this feels more like a inspiration of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-513">SCP-513</a> just that the effects of the bell are more violent.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This will describe what happened when a historical society/museum renovated it and rang it for the first time</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How DID they renovate it exactly? You can't leave that blank. While the foundation does leave some stuff away, you have to give a little bit of context.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Discovery log - This will describe the findings of the archaeological dig where the bell was found. Summarised:<br />
Discovered in the Fens near Crowland Abbey, England.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd recommend you keeping it secret since some SCPs have their locations of where they were found redacted or with a black box. THAT'S what the Foundation does to keep things secret.</p>
<p>I'm not a good criticizer nor am I a old member of SCP. I am actually new. But you should probably take these things into consideration in my opinion. I like the SCP but this has flaws.</p>

